<exercisegroup cols="2">
<title>Choosing a cofactor expansion</title>

<introduction><p>
	For each matrix,
	choose a row or column for which calculating the cofactor expansion would require the fewest minor determinant calculations.
</p></introduction>


<!-- 3 x 3 -->

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		\begin{abmatrix}{rrr}
			-4 \amp -3 \amp -6 \\
			 0 \amp  5 \amp -9 \\
			-4 \amp  9 \amp -9
		\end{abmatrix}
	</m></p></statement>

	<answer><p>
		A cofactor expansion along either the first column or the second row would involve only two minor determinant calculations,
		rather than three.
	</p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		\begin{abmatrix}{rrr}
			-7 \amp  1 \amp -4 \\
			-3 \amp -8 \amp  3 \\
			 5 \amp  0 \amp  0
		\end{abmatrix}
	</m></p></statement>

	<answer><p>
		A cofactor expansion along the third row would involve only one minor determinant calculation,
		rather than three.
	</p></answer>

</exercise>

<!-- 4 x 4 -->

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		\begin{abmatrix}{rrrr}
			-1 \amp -1 \amp  9 \amp  0 \\
			 0 \amp  3 \amp -2 \amp  8 \\
			-2 \amp -7 \amp  4 \amp -2 \\
			-3 \amp -3 \amp  7 \amp  5
		\end{abmatrix}
	</m></p></statement>

	<answer><p>
		A cofactor expansion along any of the first or second rows or the first or fourth columns would involve only three minor determinant calculations,
		rather than four.
	</p></answer>

</exercise>

<exercise>

	<statement><p><m>\displaystyle
		\begin{abmatrix}{rrrr}
			 4 \amp  0 \amp  2 \amp  1 \\
			-2 \amp  0 \amp -1 \amp -9 \\
			 4 \amp -9 \amp  8 \amp  5 \\
			 3 \amp  9 \amp  5 \amp  6
		\end{abmatrix}
	</m></p></statement>

	<answer><p>
		A cofactor expansion along the second column would involve only two minor determinant calculations,
		rather than four.
	</p></answer>

</exercise>

</exercisegroup>
